hman Benjamin Hébert after four match days. David Drysdale took third place after winning against James Heath. In 1957 Hunt (137) beat Rees (145) by 8 strokes in a 36-hole playoff. In 1935 Branch (145) beat Van Donck (149) by 4 strokes in a 36-hole playoff.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d01\", \"text\": \"Belgian Open (tennis) The Belgian Open was a WTA Tour tennis event held over three different periods during 1987–2002. The competition took place in July during 1987–1989 and 2002, and in May during 1992–1993 and 1999–2001. During 2000–2001 it was sponsored by Dutch clothing chain Mexx and renamed the \\\"Benelux Open\\\". The competition was played on outdoor clay courts. The tournament was a Tier V event in 1992 and 2001. The tournament was a Tier IV event in 1993, 1999, 2000 and 2002. Only one Belgian woman won the singles event; the then little-known Justine Henin, aged 16 in 1999.\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"Tennis\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"The Belgian Open is a professional tennis tournament held in Belgium.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Belgian Open\", \"scope\": \"sport\", \"claim\": \"The Belgian Open is associated with golf.\", \"answer\": \"Golf\", \"quote\": \"The first edition of the Belgian Knockout, which is the 53rd edition of the Belgian Open, took place from 17 to 20 May 2018 at Rinkven International Golf Club, Schilde, Antwerp.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Belgian Open\", \"scope\": \"sport\", \"claim\": \"The Belgian Open is associated with tennis.\", \"answer\": \"tennis\", \"quote\": \"Belgian Open (tennis) The Belgian Open was a WTA Tour tennis event held over three different periods during 1987–2002.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}]}"
